  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study's findings are based on a small, qualitative sample of 31 interviewees in a single metropolitan area, which may limit generalizability to other urban contexts.",
      "what": "This study analyzed the Los Angeles Mobility Wallet Pilot Program, which provided low-income participants with flexible funds for various shared transportation services. Researchers conducted interviews with 31 participants before, during, and after the one-year pilot to evaluate changes in their travel behavior and quality of life.",
      "why": "The findings demonstrate that flexible, demand-side transportation subsidies can reduce material hardship and stress while improving travel frequency, social connections, and personal autonomy for low-income residents, offering an alternative to traditional transit-only assistance."
    }
